  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New module `camcraft_geometry::outline_text`. It reads a TrueType outline font and makes a typed string into closed shapes, in mm, on the layer `text`.\n  - `ttf.rs` is our own reader, written from the public OpenType specification. It reads `cmap` formats 4 and 12, `loca`, `glyf` (simple and composite glyphs), `hmtx`, `hhea`, `maxp`, `head` and the `OS/2` cap height. Each read has a bounds check.\n  - `mod.rs` flattens the quadratic contours to lines, with a chord error of 0.005 mm or less. It then makes a `SketchData` with closed chains only.\n  - `sample_font.rs` makes a small test font in memory. It has our own glyphs, so the repository stores no font file.\n- New undoable command `InsertOutlineText` (`crates/app/src/commands/insert_outline_text.rs`). It reads the font once at construction. The profile keeps the shapes, not the font, so the project file format does not change.\n- New MCP tool `insert_outline_text` (`crates/app/src/mcp/outline_text_tools.rs`). The tool is also in `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` (generated) and in the MCP guide table.\n- These inputs are refused by name:\n  - a font that cannot be read, a CFF font (`.otf` with PostScript outlines) or a font collection;\n  - an empty text, or a character that the font does not have;\n  - outlines that cross or touch;\n  - a nested outline that runs in the same direction as the outline around it (`OutlineTextError::Winding`);\n  - a height or a spacing outside the limits;\n  - a setup that does not exist, a setup with no stock, or a name that is in use.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3072-outline-text.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is a new feature (#3072). Before this PR, typed text was only single-stroke engraving text (`insert_text`, #2679).\n\n## Review fixes\n\nRound 1:\n\n- Large curves keep the 0.005 mm chord tolerance. A curve can use up to 4096 pieces. A curve that needs more is refused.\n- Composite glyphs apply `SCALED_COMPONENT_OFFSET`. A component with both offset flags is refused.\n- Table reads use each declared table boundary. Character maps also use each declared subtable boundary.\n\nRound 2:\n\n- Nonzero winding fill. The sketch reads holes by nesting, but a TrueType font fills by the nonzero winding rule. These two readings agree only when each outline runs opposite to the innermost outline around it. `check_winding` in `outline_text/mod.rs` refuses all other arrangements by name. Thus a same-direction inner contour is never made a hole.\n- Red verification result. The branch was 106 commits behind `upstream/main`. On the old base, `blind_slot`, `corner_relief_safety` and one post-dialog UI test failed. The trial merge of the reviewer passed them. I merged `upstream/main` into the branch with a merge commit (no rebase, no conflicts). This host has a graphics adapter, so the UI suites ran. The quick gate on the final head is green.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test outline_text`: 10 passed.\n- Pin proof, round 2: `nested_outlines_follow_the_nonzero_winding_fill`. With the `check_winding` call removed, the test failed at `crates/geometry/tests/outline_text.rs:233` (the same-direction `O` was accepted). With the call restored, it passed. The test also checks that an `O` with both directions swapped still has one hole, and that `II` stays two shapes.\n- Pin proof, round 1: the four round-1 tests failed with the original reviewed source and passed with the fixes:\n  - `large_curves_measure_inside_the_chord_tolerance`\n  - `composite_offsets_use_the_component_transform`\n  - `declared_table_lengths_bound_reads_with_trailing_bytes`\n  - `declared_cmap_subtable_lengths_bound_reads`\n\nFinal head: `7bedbc7eef7482df9059d5305d9e63caa9fa881f`. Gates ran against `upstream/main` `054c1e24b` (the merged base).\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: **GREEN**. 1105 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 20.3 minutes. This includes `ui suites: lib`, `ui suites: egui_app`, `ui suites: shell`, `geometry suites: outline_text`, `app suites: insert_outline_text` and `clippy -D warnings`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: **GREEN**. 244 reached app and motion steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 38.0 minutes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The quick gate on the final head ran these suites, and all passed:\n\n- `app suites: example_catalog`\n- `app suites: example_catalog_adaptive`\n- `app suites: example_catalog_edge_work`\n- `app suites: golden_cl`\n\nThe heavy gate ran the ignored catalog cases, and all passed. No recorded program changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `graphify update`: the command is not installed on this host.\n- UI screenshots: not applicable. This PR changes no UI code.\n- Toolpath generation on the text. A toolpath from the chains of any DXF-type profile is not on main yet: #1867 does that work. The test only pins that the pocket and the contour accept the text as closed chains.\n- A real third-party font file. The tests use the generated sample font only.\n- CFF (`.otf` PostScript) fonts. These are refused by name. A CFF reader can come later as a different issue.\n- The UI. This PR adds no dialog. The command is available through MCP.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2924 changes `crates/app/src/mcp/sketch_tools.rs` (`insert_text`). This PR does not touch that file.\n- #3304 changes `crates/app/src/commands/insert_text.rs`. This PR does not touch that file. It has its own name helper.\n- These PRs touch `crates/geometry/src/lib.rs`: #3061, #2999, #2993, #2992, #2981, #2979, #2978 and #2924. Each adds a line to the module list, so the lines are different. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Typed text in a TrueType outline font becomes a profile of closed shapes (letter holes included) for a pocket, V-carve or cut-out: MCP tool `insert_outline_text`, one undo step; unreadable or CFF fonts, missing glyphs, overlapping outlines and nested outlines that the font's nonzero fill does not make holes are refused by name.\n\nFixes #3072\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
